{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTowerForward","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTowerForward","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRowSubset","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalBlockEquality","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.MarkovAssembly"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.incl_mem_rad_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.incl_mem_rad_iff","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalTowerForward.lean#L129-L145","doc":"**The tower inclusion detects the radical EXACTLY** — unconditionally, at the\nconcrete `wtrace` carrier.\n\nReflection is `mem_rad_of_incl_mem_rad` (one rewrite of `wtrace_incl`); the forward\ndirection routes through the radical identification and the branching rule.  Together:\n`H_m / rad ↪ H_{m+1} / rad`, so the Temperley–Lieb quotients are a tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.twoRow_blocks_vanish_incl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.twoRow_blocks_vanish_incl","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalTowerForward.lean#L107-L127","doc":"**Forward: the inclusion carries the radical upstairs.**\n\nIf every at-most-two-row block kills `a` downstairs, then every at-most-two-row block\nkills `heckeIncl a` upstairs — because each of its diagonal blocks IS a downstairs\nblock at an erased corner, and erasing a corner keeps the diagram at two rows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.eq_zero_of_blockPreserving_of_compress_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.eq_zero_of_blockPreserving_of_compress_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalTowerForward.lean#L87-L105","doc":"**A block-diagonal matrix whose every diagonal block vanishes is zero.**\n\nOff-block entries die by `BlockPreserving`; an on-block entry is literally an entry of\nthe corresponding compression, via `exists_insertMax_of_cellOf_top`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.rowLen_two_eq_zero_eraseCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.WtraceRadicalTwoRow.rowLen_two_eq_zero_eraseCorner","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/WtraceRadicalTowerForward.lean#L73-L85","doc":"**Erasing a corner cannot create a third row.**\n\n`eraseCorner` only removes a cell, so a cell in row 2 of the erasure was already one\nupstairs — where `rowLen 2 = 0` forbids it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}